# ML generated artifacts (regenerated by train.exe). Keep .gitkeep + manifests,
# ignore the bulky append-only streams, per-epoch checkpoints, and demo exports.
# data/*.meta.json covers pairgen recipe sidecars and shard logs live with them.
data/*.jsonl
data/*.jsonl.*
data/*.meta.json
data/opener_bias/
models/*_ckpt*.txt
models/py_linear.txt
agents/library.txt

# Run archive: keep the curated, human-readable history (config.json, elo.tsv,
# notes.md, runs/index.jsonl, agents/registry.*), but ignore each run's bulky
# results.jsonl copy (it mirrors the already-ignored data/tourney.jsonl).
runs/**/results.jsonl

# Position-oracle label pipeline (tools/label_study.ps1). The raw playout
# stores are bulky and regenerable only by replaying the campaign, so back
# them up outside git; their .meta.json sidecars (the rung-id mapping), the
# position pools, ladder specs, fitted labels, frozen ratings snapshot, and
# the study ledger are small durable records and stay committed.
data/labels/raw_train.jsonl
data/labels/raw_eval.jsonl
data/labels/*.jsonl.s*
data/labels/dry/
data/labels/logs/

# Agent Elo ranking (rank.exe). Unlike data/*.jsonl, the match store is
# deliberately KEPT: it is the never-recomputed match history the ratings are
# built from. Only per-shard temp files and the gauntlet scratch are ignored.
ranking/matches.jsonl.*
ranking/gauntlet.jsonl
ranking/climb_*.tsv

# The store is split into PARTS by who played each game (`rank.exe split`),
# listed in the committed ranking/matches.index.txt. Committed: games between
# rostered agents (matches.roster.*.jsonl, 132,769 rows / 55 MB) and games
# touching other retired agents (matches.retired_other.*.jsonl, 59,054 rows /
# 23 MB), which are kept tracked so re-rostering one of those agents stays an
# open option.
#
# Only the TD-Leaf Pass-2 screening cohort is untracked: 25 candidates were
# tried and 16 promoted, and the discarded ones left 457,611 rows / 193 MB, 89%
# of all retired rows and 71% of the whole store.
#
# Those files were DELETED 2026-08-02 to reclaim the space, on the developer's
# instruction. They were never committed and never pushed, so no copy survives
# anywhere: that population is now unrecoverable except by replaying the whole
# Pass-2 campaign. The pattern below stays so a future screening cohort's parts
# are ignored by default.
#
# NOTE, because it is easy to assume otherwise: a retired agent's games are not
# dead weight just because the agent is not in standings.tsv. Bradley-Terry
# fits every rating jointly, so a game against a retired agent is evidence about
# the ROSTERED agent that played it. Rating without these parts moves 156 of 170
# rostered agents and widens the mean error bar from 7.2 to 11 Elo (measured
# 2026-08-01). The certified ranking therefore needs the untracked parts, which
# a fresh clone does not have. See plans/store-sharding-results-1-tidy-albatross.md.
ranking/matches.retired_tdleaf_self.*.jsonl

# Screening pool (tools/tdleaf_study.ps1 -ScreenStore). Cohort games are played
# here instead of the permanent ladder, so a study's discarded candidates never
# enter it. Bulky and transient: on promotion, `rank.exe split` over this store
# separates the kept agents' games for merging into the ladder, and the rest
# stay here. Its pinned-fit outputs are already covered by ranking/*_pinned.*.
ranking/matches_screen.jsonl
ranking/matches_screen.jsonl.*
ranking/matches_screen.*.jsonl
ranking/ratings_screen.tsv
ranking/standings_screen.tsv
ranking/games_screen.tsv
ranking/report_screen.md

# One-off screening cohort store (risk-weight study, see
# plans/risk-weight-results-1-dusty-kestrel.md). Same rationale as the
# matches_screen.* block above (a study's games kept out of the permanent
# ladder) but named for this specific study rather than a reusable pool; its
# pinned-fit outputs are already covered by ranking/*_pinned.* below.
ranking/matches_risk_study.jsonl
ranking/matches_risk_study.jsonl.*
ranking/matches_risk_study.*.jsonl

# Rating outputs, regenerated from the store by `rank.exe rate` (measured
# 2026-08-01: 19.4 s over 649,434 games) and verified deterministic, so they are
# not committed. Run a rate before reading standings in a fresh clone.
ranking/ratings.tsv
ranking/standings.tsv
ranking/games.tsv
ranking/report.md
ranking/ratings_open.tsv
ranking/standings_open.tsv
ranking/games_open.tsv
ranking/report_open.md
# Pinned-fit outputs (rank.exe rate --pin) are a screening artifact of one study,
# regenerable from the store, and must never be mistaken for the canonical
# ratings/standings -- so they are not committed.
ranking/*_pinned.tsv
ranking/*_pinned.md
# Regime-balanced fit outputs (rank.exe rate --regime-balanced). A different
# question from the certified table -- "strong against the space of strategies"
# rather than "strong against this pool" -- so they are kept out of git for the
# same reason as the pinned family: nothing should be able to mistake them for
# the canonical ranking. Promoting this fit to canonical is a deliberate act
# that re-certifies every champion (see todo.md).
ranking/*_balanced.tsv
ranking/*_balanced.md

# Training hyperparameter sweeps (tools/sweep_pst.ps1): throwaway model
# checkpoints + generated report, regenerable by re-running the sweep.
# Exceptions: the vs-champion study's promoted family models (slots 94..99)
# are referenced by hash from the committed ranking/roster.txt, so they must
# travel with the repo, and vs_champ.csv is that study's durable record.
models/sweep/*
!models/sweep/vs_champ.csv
!models/sweep/slot94.txt
!models/sweep/slot95.txt
!models/sweep/slot96.txt
!models/sweep/slot97.txt
!models/sweep/slot98.txt
!models/sweep/slot99.txt
